  "result": "The decision lives in `src/hooks/shortcut-match.ts`. `matchesShortcut` compares a keydown event against a registered shortcut token list like `[\"mod\", \"k\"]`. `prefersMetaKey(platform)` decides whether `mod` means Command (meta) or Control (ctrl), and `formatShortcut` uses the same rule for display.\n\nThe keydown listener in `src/hooks/use-keyboard-shortcut.ts` reads `navigator.platform` and calls `matchesShortcut`. It also skips bare-letter shortcuts while the user is typing. The shortcuts themselves are registered through `useKeyboardShortcut` in `src/hooks/use-command-palette.ts`, with their definitions in `src/hooks/command-groups.ts`. Those registration files don't make the matching decision, so I left them out.\n\nANSWER: src/hooks/shortcut-match.ts, src/hooks/use-keyboard-shortcut.ts",
